{
"dur": 60.045,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.917,
"text": "In China, Genghis's grandson Kublai became Great Khan in 1260, after a four-year war with his own brother.",
"end": 7.192
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 7.192,
"vo_start": 7.467,
"vo_end": 14.267,
"text": "In 1271 he declared a new Chinese-style dynasty, the Yuan, and built a capital at what is now Beijing, called Khanbaliq.",
"end": 14.542
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.542,
"vo_start": 14.817,
"vo_end": 21.216,
"text": "By 1279 he had defeated the Song dynasty in the south, and for the first time all of China was ruled by Mongols.",
"end": 21.491
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.491,
"vo_start": 21.766,
"vo_end": 27.886,
"text": "Foreign visitors came to his court. The Venetian Marco Polo later claimed he served Kublai for seventeen years.",
"end": 28.161
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 28.161,
"vo_start": 28.436,
"vo_end": 37.701,
"text": "Kublai wanted Japan too. In 1274 he sent a fleet. It landed, fought, and then pulled back, and a storm wrecked many ships on the way.",
"end": 37.976
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 37.976,
"vo_start": 38.251,
"vo_end": 46.411,
"text": "In 1281 he sent an even bigger invasion, by traditional count more than a hundred thousand men. For weeks the Japanese held them on the beaches.",
"end": 46.686
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 46.686,
"vo_start": 46.961,
"vo_end": 52.467,
"text": "Then a typhoon struck and destroyed much of the fleet. The Japanese called it kamikaze, the divine wind.",
"end": 52.742
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 52.742,
"vo_start": 53.017,
"vo_end": 59.095,
"text": "His armies also failed in Vietnam and Java. Even the Mongols had limits at sea and in tropical jungle.",
"end": 60.045
}
],
